    "title": "test: cover cumulative input value range in CheckTxInput tests.",
    "user": {
      "login": "KY-U",
      "id": 90665609,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjkwNjY1NjA5",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90665609?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/KY-U",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/KY-U/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "In `Consensus::CheckTxInputs`, for every input coin, if either `coin.out.nValue` or `nValueIn` is out of range, the transaction is invalid. The current `checktxinputs_invalid_transactions_test` only cover cases with one input, so the sum `nValueIn` is always equal to `coin.out.nValue`, leaving the [following mutant](https://mutanthub.space/mutants/275) alive.\r\n```diff\r\n--- a/src/consensus/tx_verify.cpp\r\n+++ b/src/consensus/tx_verify.cpp\r\n@@ -186,1 +186,1 @@\r\n-        if (!MoneyRange(coin.out.nValue) || !MoneyRange(nValueIn)) {\r\n+        if (!MoneyRange(coin.out.nValue) && !MoneyRange(nValueIn)) {\r\n\r\n```\r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/5fda85a93b2957d68b2f89fdfe56c8608c0cacd9 adds support for multiple inputs in the test helper.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/389144324b0bb5e7c39078b59a50b738c53e7741 adds a test case with multiple valid inputs, whose sum exceed MAX_MONEY, while also having `nValueIn` != `coin.out.nValue`, killing the mutant.",
    "labels": [
      {
        "id": 62963516,
        "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw2Mjk2MzUxNg==",
